    "durationMs": 271350,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. All 27 functional tests passed, persistence was confirmed across restarts, and the database was left clean for the grading suite.\n\n**What I built** (ASP.NET Core 8 minimal API, EF Core 8 + Npgsql):\n\n- `Program.cs` — reads `DATABASE_URL` from the environment (no hard-coded credentials), registers the DbContext, maps endpoints; `start.sh` invokes a `migrate` mode that applies pending EF migrations, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`.\n- `Endpoints.cs` — all four routes with the exact contract: `POST /links` (201, URL stored unchanged, unique generated codes with retry-on-collision, 409 for duplicate custom codes), `GET /links/{code}` (404 with `{\"error\"}`), `GET /r/{code}` (302 + atomic `clicks + 1` via `ExecuteUpdateAsync`), `GET /links` (ascending creation order, `{\"items\", \"total\"}`).\n- `LinkRules.cs` / `DatabaseUrl.cs` — code validation (4–20 of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`) and generation, http/https-with-host URL validation, and PostgreSQL-URL→Npgsql connection-string parsing (including query params and URL-encoded credentials).\n- Manual JSON body parsing so malformed JSON, invalid/missing `url`, and invalid `code` all return **422** (the default minimal-API binder would have returned 400).\n- `Migrations/` (InitialCreate with unique index on code), `start.sh`, `README.md`.\n\n**Verified end-to-end**: creation, custom codes, 409/404/422 paths, redirect Location exactly matching, click increments exactly once even under 20 concurrent requests, data surviving a full server restart, and `sh start.sh` working from any working directory."
  }
